      "summaries": {
        "en": "Sherlock is an open-source OSINT tool that helps security researchers and investigators find social media accounts by username across hundreds of platforms. It works by systematically querying each site's public profile endpoints and analyzing response patterns to detect account existence. You can use it via command line to trace digital footprints during investigations, customize it with new site modules, or integrate it into automated reconnaissance workflows for cybersecurity assessments.",
        "zh": "Sherlock是一款开源OSINT工具，帮助安全研究人员通过用户名在数百个社交平台追踪账户踪迹。它通过系统化查询各网站公开资料接口并分析响应模式来检测账户存在，展示了如何利用公开API进行高效信息收集。用户可通过命令行在调查中追踪数字足迹，添加自定义平台模块扩展覆盖范围，或将其集成到自动化侦察流程中用于网络安全评估，特别适合渗透测试和数字取证场景。",
        "es": "Sherlock is an open-source OSINT tool that helps security researchers and investigators find social media accounts by username across hundreds of platforms. It works by systematically querying each site's public profile endpoints and analyzing response patterns to detect account existence. You can use it via command line to trace digital footprints during investigations, customize it with new site modules, or integrate it into automated reconnaissance workflows for cybersecurity assessments.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "sherlock stands out for cli, cti, and cybersecurity in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Sherlock is an open-source OSINT tool that helps security researchers and investigators find social media accounts by username across hundreds of platforms. It works by systematically querying each site's public profile endpoints and analyzing response patterns to detect account existence. You can use it via command line to trace digital footprints during investigations, customize it with new site modules, or integrate it into automated reconnaissance workflows for cybersecurity assessments.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/sherlock-project/sherlock for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
